  "novel": "Robin's [[teen|teen]] pop star past as Robin Sparkles was [[revealed|reveal]]. Her old music video 'Let's Go to the Mall' was [[unearthed|unearth]], and the group watched it in [[horror|horror]] and [[delight|delight]].\n\nRobin was [[embarrassed|embarrass]]. \"I was [[sixteen|sixteen]],\" she [[pleaded|plead]]. \"Everyone did [[silly|silly]] things.\"\n\nBut Barney [[played|play]] the video on [[repeat|repeat]]. Marshall [[sang|sing]] along within minutes. Ted [[memorized|memorize]] the [[dance|dance]] moves.\n\n\"This is [[hilarious|hilarious]],\" Barney [[declared|declare]]. \"You were a [[Canadian|Canadian]] pop star!\"\n\nRobin watched her [[younger|young]] self on screen, full of hope and [[naive|naive]] dreams. She had wanted to be famous. Now she was a news reporter.\n\nSome [[dreams|dream]], she realized, were like sandcastles in the sand — beautiful while they lasted, but washed away by time.",
